fact WorkItem(id: "WI-829", description: some(value: "DeferToRequirement sole-cover arm does not σ-gate a compound element: the direct-dispatch defer path forwards the frame's shallower dictionary to a deeper in-body call. DRIVEN REPRO (WI-825 /code-review, max effort): sort DHolder2 / sort HT=? / requires Desc[T=Wrap[A=HT]] / operation d2(y:HT)->Int64 = Desc.describe(wrap(wrap(y))), called DHolder2.d2(leaf()), returns Ok(Int(12)) where 122 is correct (the wi825 positive_control pins 122 for the same depth-2 shape). ROOT CAUSE: WI-825 made binding_pair_covers/sigma_pair_precise compound-aware for the FORWARDING path (build_dep_projection), but the classification path find_requires_location/find_requires_slot returns a SOLE coarse cover without consulting σ — the sole-cover arms [(only,_)] => Some(only.clone()) (typing.rs ~13354) and [only] => Some(*only) (~13124); σ is tie-break-only (pick_precise) and the dispatch trigger dispatch_spec_op_cached passes sigma=None (~18080). entry_matches_subst coarse-accepts the shallow-vs-deep compound pair via dispatch_values_match's head fallback (Wrap==Wrap, interiors ignored), so DeferToRequirement reads the wrong-depth frame dict. This is the SOLE-ENTRY compound variant of the gap WI-821 delivery-feedback already flagged (disambiguate_slot_by_sigma soft pick_precise fall-back, one site over). FIX DIRECTION: σ-gate the sole-cover selection in find_requires_location/find_requires_slot (or make the DeferToRequirement classification construct/refuse when the sole cover σ-disagrees), sharing the WI-825 compound-aware verdict. ACCEPTANCE: the driven d2 fixture measures 122; wi825/wi817/wi828 + full workspace green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-825"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-24T19:42:44Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-829", author: "user", content: "RELATED findings from the same WI-825 /code-review (σ-cover-verdict completeness), NOT fixed by the WI-825 follow-up cleanup commit — verification was cut short by a Fable-5 credit exhaustion, so most are PLAUSIBLE not driven. (1) CONFIRMED-trace: RequirementRefusal::render (typing.rs ~11424) emits the WI-821 'covers only as a wildcard / different type parameter (WI-821)' clause for the both-COMPOUND structural refusals explain_dep_refusal now collects, where neither side is a wildcard/param and the unconstrained scan (~11529, head-only is_type_param_value) names no element — misdiagnosis; NOTE wi828's assert_refusal_diagnostic requires the literal 'WI-821' + 'CT' pieces, so a render fix must update those asserts. (2) PLAUSIBLE: explain_dep_refusal mirrors only the DEP-driven entries_cover walk (~11476); an ENTRY-driven S3 FromScope σ-refusal (multi-param dep, caller binds fewer) leaves refused_entries empty → Ok(None) → silent load-clean-die-at-eval, the anti-pattern WI-828 removed, newly reachable via compound refusal. (3) PLAUSIBLE regression: the both-parameterized arm hard-refuses base/arity mismatch WITHOUT the dispatch_values_match fallthrough, dropping types_lesseq's provider-admissibility (List provides Stream) + width-tolerant acceptances — may refuse correct programs (suite green ⇒ latent). (4) PLAUSIBLE: interior param σ-bound-to-concrete hits the syntactic mixed rule → over-refusal vs the pre-fix head accept. (5) PLAUSIBLE residuals (same head-fallback class one form over, undocumented/mis-documented): bare-vs-applied same-sort (requires Desc[T=Wrap] covers any depth), and interior arrow/tuple leaves (Wrap[A=arrow1] vs Wrap[A=arrow2] via meta-ctor head match) — parameterized_parts' 'no σ-gated path carries those forms' doc claim is false for interiors (Relation[T=(tuple)] is live, WI-764). (6) PLAUSIBLE: named-args one-directional pairing is not a bijection under duplicate labels (sort_binding lists lack check_label_unique) or dual-spelled keys → a named_b component uncompared. (7) reached_carrier_matches_call (WI-653 op-requires license) + entry_sigma_matches_subst (WI-613 tie-break) both silently strictened for compounds with no test coverage.", at: "2026-07-24T05:44:26Z")
